 ],
 "notes": "'sensitive' on outputs is not visible in the normalised input, so only the output wiring is checked: an output referencing each login profile (the generated password) and one referencing each user (username). An output of a separate random_password is not the console password the login profile generates, so it fails the password-output checks. Each custom policy may be a managed aws_iam_policy attached to the group or an inline aws_iam_group_policy of the stated name; grants are read from that policy's planned JSON, declared text, or a referenced aws_iam_policy_document. A bare service wildcard (ec2:*, s3:*, budgets:* ...) is full access, so it does not count as a read-only grant; Describe*/Get*/List*/View* wildcards do. Not expressible: the rest of the negative half of 'read-only' (TF policy JSON is a string, so no none_eq over actions). Candidate review: DSV4F and GLM53F fail the *_out checks because they output a separate random_password, not the login profile password; kept. The five billing grants are core like the four support grants (parallel stated requirements), so the core share is high."
}
